# Prisma

- The schema is split by domain in `prisma/schema/*.prisma` (`base`, `organization`, `identity`, `platform`, `settings`, `workflow`, …). Add a new file per business module (`assets.prisma`, `hr.prisma`).
- Model names are singular PascalCase; tables are mapped to snake_case plurals with `@@map("asset_assignments")`. Columns keep their camelCase field names (no `@map`).
- Every tenant-owned model has `companyId String @db.Uuid` with a relation to `Company` and an index starting with `companyId`.
- IDs are `String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid`. Timestamps: `createdAt`, `updatedAt @updatedAt`; soft delete with `deletedAt DateTime?` only where the domain needs it.
- Money: `Decimal @db.Decimal(18, 2)`; rates/quantities: `@db.Decimal(18, 6)` or as the domain requires.
- Business-unique fields are unique **per company**: `@@unique([companyId, code])`.

## Migrations

- Create with `pnpm db:migrate --name <snake_case_change>`; commit the generated SQL.
- Never edit a migration that is already on `main`; add a new one instead.
- Data backfills that cannot be expressed in SQL go into a one-off script, not into the migration.

## Data access

- Inject `PrismaService`; it is the extended client with the audit extension, so creates/updates/deletes are written to `AuditLog` automatically.
- Select only the fields you need for lists (`select`), and use `include` sparingly.
- Pagination helpers live in `src/common/pagination` (`toPageArgs`, `toOrderBy`, `paginated`). Whitelist sortable columns.
- Raw SQL only through `$queryRaw` tagged templates (parameterised). Row locks for counters use `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` inside a transaction (see `NumberingService`).
- Seed data lives in `prisma/seed.ts` and must stay idempotent (`upsert`).
